; Sidecar module for the variant-visibility tests: xfail_variant_vis_hidden.scaly
; and variant_vis_glob.scaly load it via `module variant_vis_helper`. The
; harness also runs it standalone (every *.scaly here is a test), so it prints
; PASS itself; module loading ignores top-level statements.
;
; The pairing is what the tests need: `Payload` is the PAYLOAD TYPE of an arm of
; `Tagged`, and that is exactly the coincidence the old s185 rescue answered on.
; Expected: PASS

define Payload (a: int  b: int  c: int)

define Tagged union (First: Payload)

print("PASS")
